# Tests this port is not expected to pass, which script/xfstests.sh hands
# to check as -E.  Each entry is a disposition the verification record
# makes from the test's own output, and each is one of two kinds: what this
# format cannot store, and what this port refuses as DragonFly refuses it.
# A defect of the port's is never listed: it is fixed or it fails, and an
# open decision fails visibly until it is decided.  The runner counts and
# names every test this expunges, and H2_XFSTESTS_EXCLUDE=none runs them
# all, which is how a disposition is rechecked.
#
# A write of zeros is not stored, so a preallocated range is a hole, and
# FIEMAP has no unwritten extent to report where the test expects one.
generic/009
generic/092
generic/255
generic/679
generic/796
generic/797
# Dedup is on by default, so equal blocks share a physical block, and the
# test's FIBMAP overlap check is written for a filesystem without it.
generic/519
# A time is unsigned microseconds from 1970, so s_time_min is 0 and a time
# before it cannot be stored.
generic/258
# A second mount of a PFS that is already mounted is refused EBUSY, as
# DragonFly's hammer2_mount() refuses it.
generic/409
generic/410
generic/411
generic/732
